---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { contactEndpoint, analyticsEndpoint, withBase } from '../lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Colophon & privacy — Quiet Compass" description="How Quiet Compass is made, how concept evidence is labeled, and how to control local preferences and optional anonymous measurement.">
 <section><div class="shell"><span class="route">Behind the route</span><h1>Quiet on purpose.<br/>Honest by design.</h1><div class="prose"><h2 id="system">The system</h2><p>This site is built with Astro, static HTML, scoped enhancements and a small shared visual vocabulary. Fraunces supplies the expressive headings; Inter handles reading and controls. The warm palette and compass are a recurring motif, not a reason to interrupt a task.</p><p>The interface does not need a three-dimensional scene to explain itself. WebGL is not part of this edition. Project visuals are original vector interface studies, with responsive AVIF and WebP versions generated during the build.</p><h2 id="evidence">What the work represents</h2><p>Atlas, Fieldnote and Threshold are self-initiated concepts. Their artifacts are original and their sample data is synthetic. Counts refer to the illustrated interface. They are not claims about a client's revenue, conversion, user satisfaction or speed. No commissioned clients, interviews or usability-study results are implied.</p><h2 id="privacy">Privacy and preferences</h2><p>Theme, project-filter and recommendation preferences may be saved in this browser. A service worker may cache public pages and assets for offline reading. Form entries are not put in that cache or saved to local storage. A copied or downloaded brief stays on your device until you choose to share it.</p><p>{contactEndpoint?'The contact form sends the entered fields to the configured inquiry endpoint when you submit. It does not send the form as analytics.':'Message delivery is not configured in this build. Copying or saving a brief does not submit it.'}</p><p>{analyticsEndpoint?'An anonymous measurement endpoint is configured, but measurements are disabled until you opt in below. Browser Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control signals are respected.':'No analytics endpoint is connected in this build. No analytics events are sent.'} When enabled, measurements are limited to page paths without queries, event names, device category and numerical performance or interaction counts. Search text and form contents are excluded.</p><div data-preferences-tools hidden class="preferences"><label>Color theme <select data-theme-select><option value="system">Follow system</option><option value="light">Light</option><option value="dark">Dark</option></select></label><label>Anonymous measurement <select data-analytics-select><option value="denied">Off</option><option value="allowed">Allow</option></select></label></div><p data-preferences-status class="status small" role="status"></p><noscript><p>Without JavaScript, no analytics is sent and your system color preference is used.</p></noscript><h2 id="access">Access and testing</h2><p>Core reading and navigation are available without JavaScript. Comparison tools have static alternatives, optional motion respects your preferences, and visible focus states are part of the interface. Automated checks are not a certification: physical-device, assistive-technology and representative-user reviews remain separate release responsibilities.</p><p><a href={withBase('journal/reduced-motion/')}>Read the reduced-motion design note →</a></p><h2 id="release">This edition</h2><p>Build provenance and the route inventory are available in the <a href={withBase('release.json')}>public release manifest</a>. Technical implementation and remaining owner-dependent validation are documented in the repository.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/Birdi009/Vetomin">Explore the source on GitHub ↗</a></p></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
